WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:13.654
It was the last day of school before winter vacation.

2
00:00:13.655 --> 00:00:17.215
Kids were exchanging presents and saying good-bye.

3
00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:21.919
Bobby was heading toward Kids Central.

4
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:27.559
"Can you believe it's the last day of school?" Jason asked.

5
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.535
"It's not the last day of school," Bobby said.

6
00:00:31.536 --> 00:00:36.196
"The last day of school is in June."

7
00:00:36.197 --> 00:00:42.683
"It's the last school day of 2011!" Jason said.

8
00:00:42.684 --> 00:00:45.059
Miss Shelly blew her whistle.

9
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.049
"Is everyone excited for the new year?" she asked.

10
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.997
"And for vacation?"

11
00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:56.287
"Yes, but what are we doing today?" Jason interrupted.

12
00:00:56.288 --> 00:01:00.406
"It's the last day of Kids Central for the year!"

13
00:01:00.407 --> 00:01:05.307
"We're going to play a basketball game called Around the World."

14
00:01:05.308 --> 00:01:08.621
Miss Shelly held up plastic place mats.

15
00:01:08.622 --> 00:01:11.458
Each one had a letter written on it.

16
00:01:11.459 --> 00:01:17.115
"Yes! I love Around the World!" Bobby cheered.

17
00:01:17.116 --> 00:01:21.548
"These letters spell Kids Central," Miss Shelly said.

18
00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:26.771
She put the place mats on the floor around the basketball net.

19
00:01:26.772 --> 00:01:29.447
They made a big U-shape.

20
00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:32.842
"You'll start at K and shoot the basketball.

21
00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:36.087
If it goes in, you'll move to I.

22
00:01:36.088 --> 00:01:46.627
Whoever makes it closest to L wins!"

23
00:01:46.628 --> 00:01:51.387
"I'll go first!" Izzie said, rushing to letter K.

24
00:01:51.388 --> 00:01:54.211
Miss Shelly tossed her the ball.

25
00:01:54.212 --> 00:02:01.266
Everyone lined up, and Izzie took her first shot.

26
00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:05.405
"I made it!" she cheered.

27
00:02:05.406 --> 00:02:12.496
Everyone made their first two shots.

28
00:02:12.497 --> 00:02:15.405
Now they were standing at letter D.

29
00:02:15.406 --> 00:02:17.686
Izzie made her shot.

30
00:02:17.687 --> 00:02:20.987
Bobby couldn't believe how well she was doing.

31
00:02:20.988 --> 00:02:24.249
She had gotten good at basketball this year!

32
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:27.127
Nina missed her shot.

33
00:02:27.128 --> 00:02:30.009
Ethan and Jason made theirs.

34
00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:33.374
Now it was Bobby's turn.

35
00:02:33.375 --> 00:02:37.667
It was an easy shot, but Bobby felt nervous today.

36
00:02:37.668 --> 00:02:42.283
It was his last game of 2011! He shot.

37
00:02:42.284 --> 00:02:45.792
The ball hit the backboard and went in.

38
00:02:45.793 --> 00:02:54.058
"On to S!" Miss Shelly said.

39
00:02:54.059 --> 00:02:56.552
E was right in front of the net.

40
00:02:56.553 --> 00:03:01.076
Izzie, Ethan, Jason, and Bobby all made their shots.

41
00:03:01.077 --> 00:03:05.641
At N, Jason missed. He groaned.

42
00:03:05.642 --> 00:03:10.413
"I almost made it around the world!" Then he smiled.

43
00:03:10.414 --> 00:03:15.433
"But I did pretty well for me."

44
00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:18.705
Izzie, Ethan, and Bobby moved on.

45
00:03:18.706 --> 00:03:21.471
They all made T and R.

46
00:03:21.472 --> 00:03:23.989
At A, Ethan missed!

47
00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:28.881
"What?" he cried. "How did that happen?"

48
00:03:28.882 --> 00:03:32.781
He joined Nina and Jason on the floor.

49
00:03:32.782 --> 00:03:36.694
Nina cheered. "Good luck, Izzie!"

50
00:03:36.695 --> 00:03:40.536
"You can do it, Bobby!" Jason said, clapping.

51
00:03:40.537 --> 00:03:43.463
Izzie smiled at Bobby.

52
00:03:43.464 --> 00:03:46.321
"Here we go!" she said.

53
00:03:46.322 --> 00:03:48.995
She shot. "Whoo!"

54
00:03:48.996 --> 00:03:51.710
She cheered when the ball went in.

55
00:03:51.711 --> 00:03:54.598
Bobby bounced the ball.

56
00:03:54.599 --> 00:03:57.941
He couldn't get beaten by a third-grade girl.

57
00:03:57.942 --> 00:04:03.822
He shot, and . . . the ball went in!

58
00:04:03.823 --> 00:04:12.322
"The 2011 Around the World champions are Izzie and Bobby!" Miss Shelly announced.

59
00:04:12.323 --> 00:04:15.554
"Nice job, you two."

60
00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:19.151
"Thanks." Izzie was beaming.

61
00:04:19.152 --> 00:04:22.543
"Good game," Ethan called to both of them.

62
00:04:22.544 --> 00:04:24.615
Izzie turned to Bobby.

63
00:04:24.616 --> 00:04:27.071
"You'd better watch out!

64
00:04:27.072 --> 00:04:31.085
You'll have a basketball rival soon."

65
00:04:31.086 --> 00:04:34.206
"I know!" Bobby said.

66
00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:37.745
He was going to practice all vacation long.

67
00:04:37.746 --> 00:04:45.390
He wanted to beat Izzie in 2012!
